1
00:00:01,887 --> 00:00:04,557
( wood thumping )

2
00:00:04,557 --> 00:00:06,767
( Eugeo panting )

3
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:08,137
Kirito: YOU HAVE TO THINK ABOUT

4
00:00:08,137 --> 00:00:11,267
WHAT YOU’RE PUTTING
BEHIND YOUR STRIKES.

5
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:14,267
THAT’S WHAT’S GONNA TIP THINGS
IN YOUR FAVOR.

6
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:16,687
- Eugeo: WHAT DO YOU MEAN?
- Kirito: IT’S LIKE,

7
00:00:16,687 --> 00:00:19,567
FOR VOLO, IT’S THE PRIDE
AND RESPONSIBILITY

8
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:21,027
THAT COMES
WITH BEING FROM A FAMILY

9
00:00:21,027 --> 00:00:23,117
THAT TEACHES SWORDSMANSHIP.

10
00:00:23,117 --> 00:00:26,537
FOR GOLGOROSSO,
IT’S THE CONFIDENCE HE’S GOT

11
00:00:26,537 --> 00:00:28,907
FROM HAVING MUSCLES OF STEEL,

12
00:00:28,907 --> 00:00:30,707
AND FOR LIENA,

13
00:00:30,707 --> 00:00:33,287
IT’S THE PRIDE SHE TAKES
IN HER POLISHED SKILLS.

14
00:00:33,287 --> 00:00:34,957
THAT’S THE REASON
WHY THEIR ATTACKS

15
00:00:34,957 --> 00:00:36,877
ARE AS POWERFUL AS THEY ARE.

16
00:00:36,877 --> 00:00:40,337
Eugeo: THEN WHAT DO YOU THINK
I SHOULD PUT BEHIND MY SWORD?

17
00:00:40,337 --> 00:00:41,717
Kirito: THAT’S SOMETHIN’

18
00:00:41,717 --> 00:00:44,257
YOU’RE GONNA HAVE
TO FIGURE OUT YOURSELF.

19
00:00:44,257 --> 00:00:46,967
Eugeo: I’M NOT A NOBLE
OR A SWORDSMAN.

20
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:52,347
ALL I HAVE ARE MY YEARS SPENT
IN THE FOREST WIELDING AN AX,

21
00:00:52,347 --> 00:00:55,647
THAT AND THE AINCRAD STYLE
KIRITO TAUGHT ME.

22
00:00:58,567 --> 00:01:01,487
WAIT. I HAVE SOMETHING ELSE.

23
00:01:01,487 --> 00:01:03,237
♪

24
00:01:06,077 --> 00:01:07,447
( grunts )

25
00:01:09,037 --> 00:01:10,497
♪

26
00:01:10,497 --> 00:01:13,037
♪ SHINY SWORD, MY DIAMOND ♪

27
00:01:13,037 --> 00:01:14,667
( singing in Japanese )

28
00:01:25,797 --> 00:01:26,807
♪ IT’S TIME ♪

29
00:01:26,807 --> 00:01:28,637
( singing in Japanese )

30
00:02:39,157 --> 00:02:41,777
- ( wood thumping )
- ( bell tolling )

31
00:02:46,747 --> 00:02:48,877
( Eugeo sighs )

32
00:02:48,877 --> 00:02:52,797
Raios: IT SEEMS DISCIPLE EUGEO
PREFERS HACKING AWAY AT LOGS,

33
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:54,587
RATHER THAN WORKING
ON HIS FORM.

34
00:02:54,587 --> 00:02:56,917
Humbert: I RECALL
ONCE HEARING SIR EUGEO

35
00:02:56,917 --> 00:02:59,677
USED TO BE A WOODCUTTER
IN SOME BACKWOODS HOVEL.

36
00:02:59,677 --> 00:03:01,507
PERHAPS THE EXTENT
OF HIS KNOWLEDGE

37
00:03:01,507 --> 00:03:04,177
IS LIMITED TO METHODS
OF ATTACKING LUMBER.

38
00:03:04,177 --> 00:03:05,767
Raios: HOW TRULY UNFORTUNATE.

39
00:03:05,767 --> 00:03:08,017
IF THAT IS INDEED THE CASE,

40
00:03:08,017 --> 00:03:11,107
THEN AS SOMEONE WHO HAPPENS
TO TRAIN IN THE SAME DORM,

41
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:13,437
PERHAPS I SHOULD
GRACIOUSLY LEND A HAND

42
00:03:13,437 --> 00:03:15,897
AND INSTRUCT HIM
ON PROPER TECHNIQUE.

43
00:03:15,897 --> 00:03:17,697
Humbert: MY,
WHAT A CONSIDERATE THING

44
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:19,447
OF YOU TO OFFER, LORD RAIOS.

45
00:03:19,447 --> 00:03:21,737
YOU TRULY ARE
AN EXEMPLARY NOBLE.

46
00:03:21,737 --> 00:03:24,577
WHAT SAY YOU TO THAT, SIR EUGEO?

47
00:03:24,577 --> 00:03:26,577
WILL YOU ACCEPT
LORD RAIOS’S GENEROSITY

48
00:03:26,577 --> 00:03:27,867
AND HAVE HIM TRAIN YOU?

49
00:03:27,867 --> 00:03:31,077
IT’S A ONCE-IN-A-LIFETIME
OPPORTUNITY.

50
00:03:31,077 --> 00:03:32,337
( Eugeo sighs )

51
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:35,297
I APPRECIATE THE OFF--( gasps )

52
00:03:35,297 --> 00:03:37,967
Kirito: SOME UPPERCLASSMEN
USE THEIR STATUS

53
00:03:37,967 --> 00:03:39,507
AS A SOURCE OF POWER.

54
00:03:39,507 --> 00:03:41,427
Eugeo: IS THAT
WHY FIRST SEAT RAIOS

55
00:03:41,427 --> 00:03:43,637
AND SECOND SEAT HUMBERT
ARE SO STRONG?

56
00:03:43,637 --> 00:03:46,217
Kirito: IT’S A LITTLE DIFFERENT
WITH THOSE GUYS.

57
00:03:46,217 --> 00:03:48,597
THEIR EGOS ARE
ON A WHOLE ’NOTHER LEVEL.

58
00:03:48,597 --> 00:03:50,057
Eugeo: WHY DO YOU THINK THAT IS?

59
00:03:50,057 --> 00:03:51,977
Kirito: ’CAUSE THEY’RE
A COUPLE OF JERKS.

60
00:03:51,977 --> 00:03:54,187
HELL, THEY’VE BEEN LOOKING
DOWN THEIR NOSES AT PEOPLE

61
00:03:54,187 --> 00:03:55,777
SINCE THE DAY THEY WERE BORN.

62
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:58,107
THEY SURE
DON’T THINK MUCH OF US.

63
00:03:58,107 --> 00:04:00,147
FOR ONE, WE’RE FROM
OUTSIDE THE CAPITAL,

64
00:04:00,147 --> 00:04:02,737
PLUS WE DON’T HAVE
ANY KIND OF NOBLE HERITAGE.

65
00:04:02,737 --> 00:04:05,077
Eugeo: THIS MIGHT BE
A GOOD OPPORTUNITY

66
00:04:05,077 --> 00:04:09,117
FOR ME TO FIND OUT JUST
WHAT THEIR EGOS ARE CAPABLE OF.

67
00:04:09,117 --> 00:04:11,707
FORGIVE ME
FOR MISSPEAKING JUST NOW.

68
00:04:11,707 --> 00:04:13,997
I WOULD HAPPILY ACCEPT
A LESSON FROM YOU.

69
00:04:13,997 --> 00:04:16,837
Humbert: OH, HO!
HE CAN’T BE SERIOUS!

70
00:04:16,837 --> 00:04:17,837
Eugeo: I AM.

71
00:04:17,837 --> 00:04:20,007
IN FACT, I WOULD LIKE MY LESSON

72
00:04:20,007 --> 00:04:22,967
IN THE FORM OF A MATCH WITH YOU,
SIR HUMBERT,

73
00:04:22,967 --> 00:04:24,677
IF THAT ISN’T TOO MUCH TROUBLE.

74
00:04:24,677 --> 00:04:26,637
( grunts )

75
00:04:26,637 --> 00:04:29,387
( Humbert gasps )
WHY, YOU ROTTEN--

76
00:04:29,387 --> 00:04:31,807
Raios: MAY I REMIND YOU
THAT LORD HUMBERT

77
00:04:31,807 --> 00:04:34,147
IS NO SLOUCH
WHEN IT COMES TO SWORDPLAY.

78
00:04:34,147 --> 00:04:35,857
HE MAY END UP STRIKING YOU.

79
00:04:35,857 --> 00:04:39,027
Eugeo: I WOULD PREFER IF HE
STOPPED JUST SHORT OF THAT,

80
00:04:39,027 --> 00:04:42,357
BUT IF HE HITS ME,
THEN I MUST ACCEPT IT.

81
00:04:42,357 --> 00:04:45,067
THIS LESSON IS FOR MY BENEFIT,
AFTER ALL.

82
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:47,787
Humbert: VERY WELL.

83
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:50,117
I WILL BE MORE THAN HAPPY
TO DEMONSTRATE

84
00:04:50,117 --> 00:04:52,997
MY SKILLS FOR YOU, SIR EUGEO.

85
00:04:52,997 --> 00:04:53,957
LET US BEGIN THEN!

86
00:04:55,247 --> 00:04:57,167
PREPARE TO BEAR WITNESS

87
00:04:57,167 --> 00:05:00,167
TO THE ESSENCE
OF THE HIGH-NORKIAN STYLE!

88
00:05:00,167 --> 00:05:01,877
Eugeo: LIGHTNING SLASH!

89
00:05:01,877 --> 00:05:03,297
THE NORKIAN STYLE’S SECRET MOVE!

90
00:05:05,087 --> 00:05:06,677
Humbert: EN GARDE! ( yells )

91
00:05:06,677 --> 00:05:09,137
( Eugeo yells )

92
00:05:11,017 --> 00:05:12,517
( Humbert gasping )

93
00:05:16,557 --> 00:05:17,397
Raios: HUH.

94
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:24,067
Eugeo: IF IT’S A CASE
OF WHO’S STRONGER, I AM!

95
00:05:27,237 --> 00:05:30,077
Humbert: DON’T GET COCKY,
YOU COMMONER!

96
00:05:30,077 --> 00:05:32,287
Eugeo: HIS POWER SURGED.

97
00:05:32,287 --> 00:05:35,417
IS THAT WHAT HIS ARROGANCE
IS CAPABLE OF?

98
00:05:35,417 --> 00:05:37,747
Humbert: YOUR SWORD STYLE
IS A GOOD MATCH FOR YOU,

99
00:05:37,747 --> 00:05:39,797
PRIMITIVE AND UNSIGHTLY.

100
00:05:39,797 --> 00:05:41,007
( Eugeo grunting )

101
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,627
Humbert: LET’S SEE HOW YOU FARE

102
00:05:42,627 --> 00:05:44,717
AFTER I CRUSH YOUR SHOULDER.

103
00:05:44,717 --> 00:05:47,797
( Eugeo grunts )
I HAVE TO SWITCH SKILLS.

104
00:05:51,057 --> 00:05:52,017
( Humbert gasps )

105
00:05:56,097 --> 00:05:58,147
( Eugeo yells )

106
00:05:58,147 --> 00:05:59,687
- ( Humber groans )
- Raios: THAT IS ENOUGH!

107
00:06:02,027 --> 00:06:04,317
I DECLARE THIS MATCH A DRAW.

108
00:06:04,317 --> 00:06:05,817
Humbert: BUT, LORD RAIOS!

109
00:06:05,817 --> 00:06:08,117
I CAN’T WALK AWAY
FROM THIS ROGUE WITH A DRAW!

110
00:06:08,117 --> 00:06:09,907
I MUST FINISH THIS!

111
00:06:12,247 --> 00:06:13,907
Raios: STAND DOWN, HUMBERT.

112
00:06:13,907 --> 00:06:15,327
( Humbert gasps )

113
00:06:15,327 --> 00:06:16,747
( growls )

114
00:06:19,037 --> 00:06:20,207
( scabbard scrapes )

115
00:06:23,377 --> 00:06:25,587
Raios: FOR WHAT IT’S WORTH,
DISCIPLE EUGEO,

116
00:06:25,587 --> 00:06:28,047
YOUR OUTLANDISH MOVES
WERE QUITE ENTERTAINING.

117
00:06:28,047 --> 00:06:30,887
AFTER GRADUATING,
PERHAPS YOU SHOULD CONSIDER

118
00:06:30,887 --> 00:06:33,267
SEEKING A CALLING
WITH THE IMPERIAL CIRCUS.

119
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:37,897
Eugeo: THANK YOU FOR
THE SUGGESTION, DISCIPLE RAIOS.

120
00:06:40,477 --> 00:06:42,357
Raios: IN DUE TIME,
I WILL GIVE YOU

121
00:06:42,357 --> 00:06:44,277
MY OWN DEMONSTRATION
OF A NOBLEMAN’S POW--

122
00:06:44,277 --> 00:06:47,027
Eugeo: I’M FREE NOW, IF YOU ARE.

123
00:06:47,027 --> 00:06:48,317
( Humbert gasps )

124
00:06:48,317 --> 00:06:50,027
Raios: THERE IS MORE TO BATTLE

125
00:06:50,027 --> 00:06:52,987
THAN WAVING A SWORD AROUND,
YOU NAMELESS BUFFOON.

126
00:06:58,327 --> 00:06:59,457
( Eugeo sighs )

127
00:07:01,497 --> 00:07:03,547
IT’S BEEN THREE DAYS.

128
00:07:03,547 --> 00:07:06,667
THEY SHOULD HAVE TRIED
GETTING BACK AT ME BY NOW.

129
00:07:06,667 --> 00:07:08,627
I WONDER WHY THEY HAVEN’T.

130
00:07:12,717 --> 00:07:14,717
Kirito: THEY’D BE
BREAKIN’ THE RULES,

131
00:07:14,717 --> 00:07:16,727
THE SCHOOL’S
AND THE TABOO INDEX’S.

132
00:07:16,727 --> 00:07:20,097
THOSE DON’T MAKE IT EASY
TO HARASS PEOPLE.

133
00:07:20,097 --> 00:07:23,147
ON THE OTHER HAND, ANYTHING THAT
DOESN’T FALL UNDER THE RULES

134
00:07:23,147 --> 00:07:24,687
IS UP FOR DEBATE.

135
00:07:24,687 --> 00:07:26,987
THEY COULD BE LOOKIN’
FOR A LOOPHOLE.

136
00:07:26,987 --> 00:07:29,407
Eugeo: YOU THINK
THEY’D GO THAT FAR

137
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:30,907
JUST TO SPITE ME?

138
00:07:30,907 --> 00:07:32,487
Kirito: I DON’T KNOW.

139
00:07:32,487 --> 00:07:35,117
MAYBE THEY’RE NOT PLANNING
ON DOING ANYTHING.

140
00:07:35,117 --> 00:07:38,157
IT’S POSSIBLE THEY’RE
JUST TRYING TO PSYCHE YOU OUT.

141
00:07:38,157 --> 00:07:40,667
WHATEVER YOU DO,
DON’T LET IT GET TO YOU.

142
00:07:40,667 --> 00:07:42,377
NO MATTER WHAT,
YOU GOTTA STAY COOL.

143
00:07:42,377 --> 00:07:44,377
Eugeo: WHAT DID YOU SAY?

144
00:07:44,377 --> 00:07:47,087
- STAY WHAT, NOW?
- Kirito: OH, UH...

145
00:07:47,087 --> 00:07:49,967
THAT’S THE SECRET MANTRA
OF THE AINCRAD STYLE.

146
00:07:49,967 --> 00:07:53,097
IT’S PRETTY MUCH THE SAME
AS SAYING, "STAY CALM."

147
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:55,597
YOU CAN ALSO USE IT
TO SAY GOODBYE TO SOMEONE.

148
00:07:55,597 --> 00:07:57,807
IT’S LIKE ANOTHER WAY
OF SAYING, "SEE YOU LATER."

149
00:07:57,807 --> 00:08:00,227
Eugeo: OH. OKAY!

150
00:08:00,227 --> 00:08:01,227
I’LL REMEMBER THAT.

151
00:08:01,227 --> 00:08:02,767
"STAY COOL."

152
00:08:02,767 --> 00:08:04,817
WHAT AN UNUSUAL THING TO SAY.

153
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:06,357
STAY COOL? BIZARRE.

154
00:08:06,357 --> 00:08:08,147
Kirito: ALL RIGHT,
I’M GONNA GO HIT THE SACK.

155
00:08:08,147 --> 00:08:08,897
Eugeo: AND WHY "COOL"?

156
00:08:11,567 --> 00:08:14,027
Kirito: OH, HEY,
BY THE WAY, ABOUT TOMORROW,

157
00:08:14,027 --> 00:08:15,867
I HAVE TO RUN SOME ERRANDS,
SO YOU’RE ON YOUR--

158
00:08:15,867 --> 00:08:17,657
Eugeo: OH, NO, YOU DON’T!

159
00:08:17,657 --> 00:08:20,667
WE PROMISED TIESE AND RONIE
WE’D TAKE THEM OUT FOR A PICNIC,

160
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:22,787
AND BY "WE," I MEAN US,
SO IF YOU THINK

161
00:08:22,787 --> 00:08:24,167
YOU CAN GET OUT OF IT,
YOU’RE MISTAKEN.

162
00:08:24,167 --> 00:08:25,917
( Kirito sighs )

163
00:08:25,917 --> 00:08:27,627
Eugeo: THEY’LL BE HERE
AT 9:00 SHARP,

164
00:08:27,627 --> 00:08:30,257
SO MAKE SURE YOU’RE READY
TO LEAVE BY THEN. YOU GOT IT?

165
00:08:30,257 --> 00:08:31,627
Kirito: OKAY, OKAY.

166
00:08:31,627 --> 00:08:34,297
DO ME A FAVOR, THOUGH,
AND WAKE ME UP AT 8:00.

167
00:08:34,297 --> 00:08:36,307
I NEED TO CATCH UP
ON SOME SLEEP.

168
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:38,137
Eugeo: NO! 8:00’S WAY TOO LATE!

169
00:08:38,137 --> 00:08:40,347
MAKE IT 7:30!

170
00:08:40,347 --> 00:08:42,057
AND STAY COOL.

171
00:08:42,057 --> 00:08:43,437
Kirito: I KNOW I TOLD YOU

172
00:08:43,437 --> 00:08:45,187
THAT PHRASE
IS LIKE SAYING, "BYE,"

173
00:08:45,187 --> 00:08:47,777
BUT IT’S NOT SOMETHING YOU SAY
TO SOMEONE GOIN’ TO BED.

174
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:48,857
Eugeo: WHY NOT?

175
00:08:48,857 --> 00:08:51,027
Kirito: ’CAUSE YOU DON’T.

176
00:08:51,027 --> 00:08:53,947
YOU USE IT WHEN YOU’RE REALLY
SAYING GOODBYE TO SOMEONE.

177
00:08:53,947 --> 00:08:55,237
Eugeo: OH.

178
00:08:55,237 --> 00:08:57,027
WHAT A COMPLICATED PHRASE.

179
00:09:06,247 --> 00:09:11,337
IF WHAT KIRITO SAID IS TRUE,
ARE HUMBERT AND RAIOS CAPABLE

180
00:09:11,337 --> 00:09:14,547
OF SIDESTEPPING THE LAWS
OF THE AXIOM CHURCH?

181
00:09:14,547 --> 00:09:16,387
( sighs ) WHAT AM I SAYING?

182
00:09:17,967 --> 00:09:20,267
YOU CAN’T EVEN DOUBT
THE TABOO INDEX,

183
00:09:20,267 --> 00:09:21,517
MUCH LESS DISOBEY IT.

184
00:09:21,517 --> 00:09:24,477
IF THERE WERE A WAY AROUND IT,

185
00:09:24,477 --> 00:09:26,437
I COULD HAVE DONE SOMETHING

186
00:09:26,437 --> 00:09:30,987
INSTEAD OF STAND THERE
AND WATCH ALICE GET TAKEN AWAY.

187
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:34,107
WHY COULDN’T I DISOBEY
WHEN I HAD THE CHANCE?

188
00:09:35,277 --> 00:09:37,867
♪

189
00:09:41,077 --> 00:09:42,197
ALICE.

190
00:09:44,497 --> 00:09:47,207
( birds chirping )

191
00:09:47,207 --> 00:09:48,497
( frog chirping )

192
00:09:48,497 --> 00:09:51,167
Tiese: EUGEO, ARE YOU LISTENING?

193
00:09:51,167 --> 00:09:52,467
EUGEO?

194
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:54,337
Eugeo: HUH? SORRY.

195
00:09:54,337 --> 00:09:57,337
I MISSED THAT LAST PART.
YOU WERE SAYING?

196
00:09:57,337 --> 00:09:59,007
( Tiese sighs )
YOU DIDN’T HEAR A SINGLE WORD.

197
00:09:59,007 --> 00:10:00,767
Eugeo: I’M SORRY. I JUST--

198
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:03,597
I WAS JUST ADMIRING
HOW BEAUTIFUL THE FOREST WAS.

199
00:10:03,597 --> 00:10:06,187
IT HAS ANIMALS
I’VE NEVER SEEN BEFORE.

200
00:10:06,187 --> 00:10:07,227
Tiese: REALLY?

201
00:10:07,227 --> 00:10:09,687
Eugeo: YEAH, LIKE THAT ONE.

202
00:10:09,687 --> 00:10:12,987
Tiese: OH, THAT? THAT’S JUST
A PLAIN OLD GOLDEN FLYING FOX.

203
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:15,027
DON’T TELL ME
YOU’VE NEVER SEEN ONE.

204
00:10:15,027 --> 00:10:17,107
THEY’RE IN EVERY TREE
IN THE CAPITAL.

205
00:10:17,107 --> 00:10:19,737
Eugeo: OH, RIGHT.
I GUESS YOU’D BE USED TO THEM,

206
00:10:19,737 --> 00:10:21,487
SINCE YOU WERE BORN
AND RAISED HERE.

207
00:10:21,487 --> 00:10:22,577
Tiese: THAT’S TRUE.

208
00:10:22,577 --> 00:10:24,077
Eugeo: DO YOUR FOLKS
LIVE NEARBY?

209
00:10:24,077 --> 00:10:26,117
Tiese: NO.
THEY LIVE IN DISTRICT EIGHT.

210
00:10:26,117 --> 00:10:28,577
IT’S A BIT OF A WAYS AWAY
FROM WHERE WE ARE IN FIVE.

211
00:10:28,577 --> 00:10:29,997
Eugeo: OH. YOU DON’T SAY.

212
00:10:29,997 --> 00:10:32,127
UH...

213
00:10:32,127 --> 00:10:35,127
HANG ON. IF I’M NOT MISTAKEN,

214
00:10:35,127 --> 00:10:37,717
DON’T YOU COME
FROM A FAMILY OF NOBLES?

215
00:10:37,717 --> 00:10:39,427
I THOUGHT ALL OF THE MANSIONS

216
00:10:39,427 --> 00:10:41,557
WERE IN DISTRICTS
THREE AND FOUR.

217
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:43,677
Tiese: ONLY NOBLES
WHO ARE FOURTH RANK OR HIGHER

218
00:10:43,677 --> 00:10:45,097
GET TO LIVE IN THAT DISTRICT.

219
00:10:45,097 --> 00:10:47,767
MY FATHER IS
A SIXTH-RANK NOBLEMAN.

220
00:10:47,767 --> 00:10:50,357
THEREFORE, HE HAS
NO JUDICIAL AUTHORITY.

221
00:10:50,357 --> 00:10:51,857
Eugeo: I DIDN’T KNOW THAT.

222
00:10:51,857 --> 00:10:53,477
I THOUGHT THAT WAS
SOMETHING EVERY NOBLE HAS.

223
00:10:53,477 --> 00:10:55,317
Tiese: CERTAINLY NOT!

224
00:10:55,317 --> 00:10:58,527
ONLY NOBLES FOURTH RANK OR
HIGHER ARE GRANTED THAT POWER,

225
00:10:58,527 --> 00:11:00,697
WHEREAS NOBLES WHO ARE
RANKED FIFTH AND LOWER

226
00:11:00,697 --> 00:11:03,617
MUST ADHERE TO THE JUDGMENT
OF THOSE OF HIGHER RANKING!

227
00:11:03,617 --> 00:11:05,497
Eugeo: OH. INTERESTING.

228
00:11:07,497 --> 00:11:09,707
Tiese: UH, ANYWAY...

229
00:11:09,707 --> 00:11:11,417
THAT’S WHY SOMEONE LIKE MYSELF,

230
00:11:11,417 --> 00:11:13,417
AN HEIR TO A SIXTH-RANK HOUSE,

231
00:11:13,417 --> 00:11:16,217
IS AN ARISTOCRAT IN NAME ONLY.

232
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:18,127
IN THAT SENSE, OUR LIFESTYLE

233
00:11:18,127 --> 00:11:20,427
IS REALLY NO DIFFERENT
FROM MOST PEOPLE’S.

234
00:11:20,427 --> 00:11:22,717
Eugeo: OH. REALLY?

235
00:11:22,717 --> 00:11:24,097
Kirito: OKAY,
SO IF YOUR OPPONENT

236
00:11:24,097 --> 00:11:25,927
WANTS TO GET THE DROP ON YOU
FROM ABOVE

237
00:11:25,927 --> 00:11:27,597
WITH A HIGH-NORKIAN
STYLE ATTACK,

238
00:11:27,597 --> 00:11:29,267
THERE’S TWO TYPES OF STRIKES

239
00:11:29,267 --> 00:11:31,647
YOU GOTTA BE READY
TO DEFEND YOURSELF AGAINST.

240
00:11:31,647 --> 00:11:34,147
THEY ARE A STRIKE FROM ABOVE

241
00:11:34,147 --> 00:11:36,067
OR DIAGONALLY TO THE RIGHT.

242
00:11:36,067 --> 00:11:37,567
IF THEY DO ANYTHING ELSE,

243
00:11:37,567 --> 00:11:39,527
THAT MEANS THEY’RE GONNA
SWITCH UP THEIR FOOTING,

244
00:11:39,527 --> 00:11:41,617
SO YOU’LL STILL
HAVE TIME TO BLOCK IT.

245
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:43,117
( Eugeo chuckles )

246
00:11:43,117 --> 00:11:46,787
MAN, I’M STUFFED!

247
00:11:49,577 --> 00:11:53,247
Tiese: UM, IF IT WOULD BE
ALL RIGHT WITH YOU TWO,

248
00:11:53,247 --> 00:11:56,337
WE’D LIKE TO GET
YOUR THOUGHTS ON SOMETHING.

249
00:11:56,337 --> 00:11:59,337
IT’S ABOUT FRENICA,
OUR ROOMMATE AT THE DORMITORY.

250
00:11:59,337 --> 00:12:01,467
( both sigh )

251
00:12:01,467 --> 00:12:04,217
Ronie: THE ELITE DISCIPLE
WHOM SHE UNFORTUNATELY IS FORCED

252
00:12:04,217 --> 00:12:07,307
TO SERVE UNDER
IS A RATHER CRUDE INDIVIDUAL.

253
00:12:07,307 --> 00:12:09,347
OVER THE PAST FEW DAYS,

254
00:12:09,347 --> 00:12:12,687
HE’S BEEN GIVING HER ORDERS THAT
GO WAY BEYOND INAPPROPRIATE.

255
00:12:12,687 --> 00:12:15,227
Eugeo: HIS RANKING IS NO EXCUSE.

256
00:12:15,227 --> 00:12:18,437
IF HE’S MAKING HER DO THINGS
THAT VIOLATE THE SCHOOL’S RULES,

257
00:12:18,437 --> 00:12:19,737
HE SHOULD BE REPORTED.

258
00:12:19,737 --> 00:12:21,657
Tiese: THAT’S JUST IT.

259
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:24,447
TECHNICALLY,
THEY’RE NOT VIOLATIONS,

260
00:12:24,447 --> 00:12:28,197
BUT THE DEMANDS HE MAKES OF
A FEMALE STUDENT ARE SO OBSCENE.

261
00:12:28,197 --> 00:12:30,617
Eugeo: YOU DON’T
HAVE TO SAY ANY MORE.

262
00:12:30,617 --> 00:12:33,747
THE PROBLEM IS, THE ONLY WAY
TO CHANGE FRENICA’S MENTOR

263
00:12:33,747 --> 00:12:35,707
IS TO GET THE APPROVAL
OF HER CURRENT ONE.

264
00:12:35,707 --> 00:12:38,457
CAN YOU TELL US HIS NAME?

265
00:12:38,457 --> 00:12:41,797
( Tiese sighs ) YES.

266
00:12:41,797 --> 00:12:45,637
IT’S SECOND SEAT ELITE DISCIPLE,
HUMBERT ZIZEK.

267
00:12:45,637 --> 00:12:47,137
Kirito: I’M NOT SURPRISED.

268
00:12:47,137 --> 00:12:48,807
( both gasp )

269
00:12:48,807 --> 00:12:52,227
Eugeo: A FEW DAYS AGO, I HAD
A SPARRING MATCH WITH HUMBERT

270
00:12:52,227 --> 00:12:54,977
IN THE TRAINING HALL.
WE ENDED IT IN A DRAW.

271
00:12:54,977 --> 00:12:58,937
IN FACT, HE SEEMED
PRETTY UPSET BY THAT.

272
00:12:58,937 --> 00:13:03,237
MY GUESS IS HE’S TAKING
HIS FRUSTRATIONS OUT ON FRENICA.

273
00:13:03,237 --> 00:13:05,157
Ronie: HE’S DOING THIS
OUT OF REVENGE?

274
00:13:05,157 --> 00:13:06,907
HOW COULD HE BE SO CRUEL?

275
00:13:08,447 --> 00:13:10,367
Tiese: I JUST
CAN’T UNDERSTAND IT.

276
00:13:10,367 --> 00:13:14,707
WE LIVE IN A LARGER HOUSE
THAN MOST OTHER CIVILIANS

277
00:13:14,707 --> 00:13:17,167
AND ENJOY
SOME ADDITIONAL PRIVILEGES,

278
00:13:17,167 --> 00:13:19,457
BUT MY FATHER
WOULD ALWAYS REMIND ME

279
00:13:19,457 --> 00:13:22,337
THAT WE SHOULD NEVER
TAKE THOSE THINGS FOR GRANTED.

280
00:13:22,337 --> 00:13:25,257
HE’D SAY WE WERE OBLIGED
TO ENSURE EVERYONE,

281
00:13:25,257 --> 00:13:26,677
NO MATTER THEIR STATION,

282
00:13:26,677 --> 00:13:29,217
COULD LIVE
A HAPPY AND PEACEFUL LIFE.

283
00:13:29,217 --> 00:13:32,017
AND IF WAR BROKE OUT,
IT’S OUR DUTY

284
00:13:32,017 --> 00:13:35,557
TO TAKE UP OUR SWORDS FIRST
AND PROTECT THE WEAK.

285
00:13:35,557 --> 00:13:37,727
AND YET,
BECAUSE OF THE HEARTLESS ORDERS

286
00:13:37,727 --> 00:13:40,027
THAT WERE ISSUED BY A NOBLE,

287
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:43,397
FRENICA COULDN’T HELP BUT CRY
HERSELF TO SLEEP LAST NIGHT.

288
00:13:43,397 --> 00:13:47,487
IT’S NOT RIGHT. HOW CAN
SOMETHING LIKE THIS BE ALLOWED?

289
00:13:47,487 --> 00:13:49,787
( sighs )

290
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:51,157
THANK YOU.

291
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,617
Kirito: THERE’S A PHRASE
IN THE SACRED TONGUE

292
00:13:54,617 --> 00:13:56,167
THAT COMES TO MIND,

293
00:13:56,167 --> 00:13:57,957
WHICH--LET’S SEE.

294
00:13:57,957 --> 00:14:02,377
IT’S PRONOUNCED
NOBLESSE OBLIGE, I THINK.

295
00:14:02,377 --> 00:14:06,677
BASICALLY IT MEANS
WHOEVER’S GOT THE POWER

296
00:14:06,677 --> 00:14:08,887
SHOULD USE IT
FOR THE SAKE OF THE VULNERABLE,

297
00:14:08,887 --> 00:14:11,307
JUST LIKE YOUR FATHER SAID.

298
00:14:11,307 --> 00:14:13,347
IT’S A CODE OF HONOR,

299
00:14:13,347 --> 00:14:16,397
AND THAT KIND OF HONOR
IS MORE IMPORTANT

300
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:19,267
THAN ANY LAW OR CUSTOM.

301
00:14:19,267 --> 00:14:21,437
THERE ARE THINGS
YOU JUST SHOULDN’T DO,

302
00:14:21,437 --> 00:14:23,607
EVEN IF THERE’S
NO LAW AGAINST ’EM.

303
00:14:23,607 --> 00:14:27,907
AT THE SAME TIME, THERE MIGHT
BE STUFF YOU SHOULD DO,

304
00:14:27,907 --> 00:14:30,197
EVEN IF THE LAWS
SAY YOU SHOULDN’T.

305
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:33,747
Ronie: I THINK I UNDERSTAND

306
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:35,657
WHAT IT IS YOU’RE SAYING.

307
00:14:35,657 --> 00:14:37,787
IF I’M HEARING YOU CORRECTLY...

308
00:14:37,787 --> 00:14:40,627
THE TABOO INDEX
DOESN’T COVER EVERYTHING.

309
00:14:40,627 --> 00:14:42,797
IN CASES LIKE THIS ONE,

310
00:14:42,797 --> 00:14:45,337
WE HAVE TO USE
OUR OWN PERSONAL SENSE

311
00:14:45,337 --> 00:14:46,797
OF WHAT’S RIGHT
AND WHAT’S WRONG.

312
00:14:46,797 --> 00:14:49,467
INSTEAD OF BLINDLY OBEYING LAWS,

313
00:14:49,467 --> 00:14:53,557
WE NEED TO ASK WHY THEY EXIST
AND IF THEY’RE EVEN HONORABLE.

314
00:14:53,557 --> 00:14:54,807
THAT SELF-REFLECTION

315
00:14:54,807 --> 00:14:57,897
IS MORE IMPORTANT
THAN JUST BLIND FAITH.

316
00:14:57,897 --> 00:15:00,147
Kirito: YUP!
THAT’S EXACTLY RIGHT.

317
00:15:00,147 --> 00:15:01,727
IT’S SUPER IMPORTANT TO LEARN

318
00:15:01,727 --> 00:15:03,527
HOW TO ACT AND THINK
FOR YOURSELF.

319
00:15:03,527 --> 00:15:05,527
THAT’S WORTH MORE
THAN THE BEST SWORD

320
00:15:05,527 --> 00:15:07,647
OR THE FLASHIEST MOVE.

321
00:15:07,647 --> 00:15:10,737
EVEN THOUGH HUMBERT DIDN’T
TECHNICALLY BREAK THE RULES,

322
00:15:10,737 --> 00:15:13,407
WHAT HE DID IS STILL 100% WRONG.

323
00:15:13,407 --> 00:15:16,657
SOMEONE’S GOTTA HOLD HIM
ACCOUNTABLE FOR THAT.

324
00:15:16,657 --> 00:15:19,827
IN THIS CASE, IT LOOKS
LIKE IT’S UP TO US TO.

325
00:15:19,827 --> 00:15:23,667
Eugeo: RIGHT.
WE’LL GO AND SORT THIS OUT.

326
00:15:25,797 --> 00:15:28,007
Raios: WELL, WELL.

327
00:15:28,007 --> 00:15:32,387
TO WHAT DO WE OWE THE PLEASURE
OF THIS VISIT, DISCIPLE EUGEO?

328
00:15:32,387 --> 00:15:35,467
AND ON THE EVENING
OF OUR DAY OF REST, NO LESS.

329
00:15:35,467 --> 00:15:38,727
Eugeo: I’VE COME TO REPORT
A TROUBLING RUMOR.

330
00:15:38,727 --> 00:15:41,687
UNFORTUNATELY,
IT CONCERNS DISCIPLE ZIZEK.

331
00:15:41,687 --> 00:15:44,187
I THOUGHT I’D BRING THIS
TO YOUR ATTENTION

332
00:15:44,187 --> 00:15:46,897
BEFORE IT DAMAGED
HIS STELLAR REPUTATION.

333
00:15:46,897 --> 00:15:48,607
Humbert: ARE YOU MOCKING ME?!

334
00:15:48,607 --> 00:15:50,447
Raios: OH, MY.

335
00:15:50,447 --> 00:15:52,117
I MUST SAY I’M SURPRISED.

336
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:54,537
I WOULDN’T HAVE
EXPECTED THIS FROM YOU.

337
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:56,617
HOW THOUGHTFUL OF YOU
TO BE CONCERNED

338
00:15:56,617 --> 00:15:58,997
FOR THE SAKE
OF MY FRIEND’S GOOD NAME.

339
00:15:58,997 --> 00:16:01,827
HOWEVER, I’M AFRAID
I HAVE NO IDEA

340
00:16:01,827 --> 00:16:04,287
WHAT THIS RUMOR
YOU SPEAK OF COULD BE.

341
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:10,507
ALONG WITH THE NATURE
OF THESE CLAIMS,

342
00:16:10,507 --> 00:16:13,137
I MUST ASK WHERE YOU
ACQUIRED THIS INFORMATION.

343
00:16:13,137 --> 00:16:14,847
Eugeo: FROM LORD ZIZEK’S PAGE,

344
00:16:14,847 --> 00:16:17,217
ALONG WITH THE GIRLS
WHO ROOM WITH HER.

345
00:16:17,217 --> 00:16:18,977
AS FAR AS THE CLAIMS
ARE CONCERNED,

346
00:16:18,977 --> 00:16:22,727
THEY SAY LORD ZIZEK
HAS BEEN ISSUING PERVERSE ORDERS

347
00:16:22,727 --> 00:16:25,357
TO HIS PAGE, FRENICA.

348
00:16:25,357 --> 00:16:27,857
Raios: WHAT ARE
THESE "PERVERSE ORDERS"?

349
00:16:27,857 --> 00:16:30,697
I’M NOT FOLLOWING WHAT IT IS
YOU’RE GETTING AT, SIR EUGEO.

350
00:16:30,697 --> 00:16:32,867
WHICH OF THE SCHOOL’S
REGULATIONS

351
00:16:32,867 --> 00:16:34,947
HAS HE VIOLATED SPECIFICALLY?

352
00:16:34,947 --> 00:16:36,577
( Eugeo gasps )

353
00:16:36,577 --> 00:16:38,537
( sighs )

354
00:16:38,537 --> 00:16:42,037
SIR, EVEN IF SOMETHING ISN’T
SPECIFICALLY FORBIDDEN HERE,

355
00:16:42,037 --> 00:16:44,787
DO YOU NOT AGREE THERE ARE
THINGS AN ELITE DISCIPLE

356
00:16:44,787 --> 00:16:47,297
SHOULD NEVER DO
AS A PRIMARY TRAINEE’S MENTOR?

357
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:50,547
Raios: OH, HO!
I CAN TELL THIS UPSETS YOU.

358
00:16:50,547 --> 00:16:53,087
NOW THEN, WHAT EXACTLY
ARE YOU INSINUATING

359
00:16:53,087 --> 00:16:55,347
HUMBERT FORCED FRENICA TO DO?

360
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:57,177
Eugeo: I COULDN’T SAY.

361
00:16:57,177 --> 00:16:59,807
Raios: WELL,
WHAT SAY YOU, HUMBERT?

362
00:16:59,807 --> 00:17:01,387
DO YOU HAVE ANY IDEA

363
00:17:01,387 --> 00:17:03,517
WHAT IT IS SIR EUGEO
COULD BE REFERRING TO?

364
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:07,607
Humbert: NOT EVEN THE FOGGIEST!

365
00:17:07,607 --> 00:17:10,987
TRY AS I MIGHT, I CAN’T MAKE
HEADS NOR TAILS OF IT.

366
00:17:10,987 --> 00:17:12,817
IT IS TRUE THAT I ASKED HER

367
00:17:12,817 --> 00:17:14,987
TO PERFORM
SOME MENIAL TASKS FOR ME.

368
00:17:14,987 --> 00:17:17,777
BUT EVER SINCE MY DUEL
WITH SIR EUGEO,

369
00:17:17,777 --> 00:17:21,157
WHICH REGRETTABLY ENDED
IN A DRAW, I’M A CHANGED MAN

370
00:17:21,157 --> 00:17:24,117
AND HAVE IMMERSED MYSELF
FULLY IN MY TRAINING!

371
00:17:24,117 --> 00:17:27,377
WHY, I’VE BEEN USING MUSCLES
I DID NOT KNOW I HAD,

372
00:17:27,377 --> 00:17:30,257
AND, AS A RESULT,
MY BODY ACHED SO BADLY.

373
00:17:30,257 --> 00:17:32,337
IN SUCH A HUMBLED STATE
AS I WAS IN,

374
00:17:32,337 --> 00:17:34,377
I HAD NO CHOICE BUT TO ASK HER

375
00:17:34,377 --> 00:17:36,507
TO MASSAGE ME EVERY NIGHT
WHILE I BATHED.

376
00:17:36,507 --> 00:17:38,007
( Eugeo gasps )

377
00:17:38,007 --> 00:17:39,847
Humbert: I WAS CONCERNED
SHE WOULD SOIL HER UNIFORM,

378
00:17:39,847 --> 00:17:42,017
SO I GRACIOUSLY
HAD HER STRIP DOWN

379
00:17:42,017 --> 00:17:43,807
AND MASSAGE ME
IN HER UNDERGARMENTS.

380
00:17:43,807 --> 00:17:46,857
HONESTLY, I CAN’T
FOR THE LIFE OF ME UNDERSTAND

381
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:48,937
HOW ANYONE
COULD THINK THAT PERVERSE.

382
00:17:53,107 --> 00:17:57,527
Eugeo: BECAUSE OF YOUR BEHAVIOR,
FRENICA HAS BEEN BESIDE HERSELF.

383
00:17:57,527 --> 00:18:00,657
IF YOU CONTINUE HARASSING HER,
I WILL BE FORCED

384
00:18:00,657 --> 00:18:03,657
TO BRING IT TO THE ATTENTION
OF OUR INSTRUCTORS.

385
00:18:03,657 --> 00:18:04,997
I HOPE YOU UNDERSTAND.

386
00:18:04,997 --> 00:18:06,747
- Humbert: WHY, YOU...
- ( Raios claps )

387
00:18:10,547 --> 00:18:13,587
Raios: I APPRECIATE THE WARNING,
DISCIPLE EUGEO.

388
00:18:13,587 --> 00:18:15,967
DO WHATEVER YOU FEEL IS RIGHT.

389
00:18:17,047 --> 00:18:18,887
( Eugeo grunts )

390
00:18:18,887 --> 00:18:21,007
Kirito: DON’T LET
THOSE JERKS GET TO YOU.

391
00:18:21,007 --> 00:18:23,847
Eugeo: I DON’T KNOW
HOW YOU KEPT SO CALM.

392
00:18:23,847 --> 00:18:26,727
I THOUGHT I WAS GOING
TO LOSE IT IN THERE.

393
00:18:26,727 --> 00:18:29,107
Kirito: LUCKY FOR THEM,
YOU DIDN’T HAVE YOUR SWORD.

394
00:18:29,107 --> 00:18:31,277
WELL, AT LEAST,
NOW I’M PRETTY SURE

395
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:33,987
THEY’RE UP TO SOMETHING MORE
THAN JUST BEING CREEPS.

396
00:18:33,987 --> 00:18:35,737
- Eugeo: WHAT?
- Kirito: I GET THE FEELING

397
00:18:35,737 --> 00:18:37,777
THE REASON THEY’RE GOING
TO ALL THIS TROUBLE

398
00:18:37,777 --> 00:18:39,067
IS TO SET A TRAP FOR YOU.

399
00:18:39,067 --> 00:18:40,367
Eugeo: REALLY?

400
00:18:40,367 --> 00:18:42,117
Kirito: YEAH. LOOK,

401
00:18:42,117 --> 00:18:45,207
IF YOU’D TAKEN THEIR BAIT AND
STARTED GOING OFF ON HUMBERT,

402
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:48,747
THEY COULD HAVE ACCUSED YOU
OF BEING DISRESPECTFUL TO THEM,

403
00:18:48,747 --> 00:18:51,457
AND THEY’D BE IN THEIR RIGHTS
TO PUNISH YOU. YOU SEE?

404
00:18:51,457 --> 00:18:53,457
( Eugeo sighs )

405
00:18:53,457 --> 00:18:56,757
( Kirito sighs ) DON’T WORRY.

406
00:18:56,757 --> 00:19:00,347
IF HUMBERT DOESN’T STOP
MESSING WITH FRENICA, HE’LL PAY.

407
00:19:00,347 --> 00:19:02,927
FOR NOW, ALL WE CAN DO
IS TELL THE TEACHERS,

408
00:19:02,927 --> 00:19:04,677
SO STAY SHARP,
AND KEEP YOUR EYES OPEN.

409
00:19:06,347 --> 00:19:08,017
Eugeo: ALL RIGHT. I’LL DO THAT.

410
00:19:08,017 --> 00:19:10,977
Kirito: AND, EUGEO, IF
THOSE GUYS SAY ANYTHING TO YOU

411
00:19:10,977 --> 00:19:13,477
WHEN I’M NOT AROUND,
TRY NOT TO GET YOURSELF

412
00:19:13,477 --> 00:19:15,237
ALL RILED UP
LIKE YOU DID BACK THERE.

413
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:17,277
Eugeo: I-I WON’T. I PROMISE.

414
00:19:17,277 --> 00:19:19,567
I’LL JUST, YOU KNOW, STAY COOL.

415
00:19:19,567 --> 00:19:20,567
Kirito: EXACTLY.

416
00:19:20,567 --> 00:19:23,237
STAY COOL ALWAYS.

417
00:19:24,907 --> 00:19:26,787
Tiese: ALLOW ME
TO MAKE MY REPORT!

418
00:19:27,867 --> 00:19:29,917
ALL CHORES ARE DONE.

419
00:19:29,917 --> 00:19:32,037
THE ASSIGNED CLEANING
HAS ALSO BEEN COMPLETED.

420
00:19:32,037 --> 00:19:34,127
Eugeo: GOOD WORK, AS USUAL.

421
00:19:34,127 --> 00:19:35,957
I REALLY APPRECIATE IT.

422
00:19:35,957 --> 00:19:37,967
Tiese: OH, IT’S NOTHING!
I’M YOUR PAGE, AFTER ALL.

423
00:19:37,967 --> 00:19:41,177
Eugeo: BY THE WAY,
IF YOU HAVE THE TIME,

424
00:19:41,177 --> 00:19:43,597
I’D LIKE TO TALK TO YOU
ABOUT SOMETHING.

425
00:19:43,597 --> 00:19:45,927
YOU DON’T HAVE TO STAND.
PLEASE, SIT DOWN.

426
00:19:45,927 --> 00:19:47,887
( Tiese gasps )

427
00:19:54,147 --> 00:19:56,317
VERY WELL. IF YOU INSIST.

428
00:20:03,117 --> 00:20:04,827
Eugeo: UH...

429
00:20:06,537 --> 00:20:07,997
( clears throat )

430
00:20:07,997 --> 00:20:10,367
IT’S ABOUT FRENICA.

431
00:20:10,367 --> 00:20:12,957
I HAD A TALK WITH HUMBERT
ABOUT HER YESTERDAY.

432
00:20:12,957 --> 00:20:14,377
Tiese: DID YOU, REALLY?!

433
00:20:14,377 --> 00:20:16,957
Eugeo: I DOUBT HE WANTS
TO GET INTO ANY TROUBLE,

434
00:20:16,957 --> 00:20:19,967
SO I’M PRETTY SURE HE WON’T BE
HARASSING HER ANYMORE.

435
00:20:19,967 --> 00:20:21,637
Tiese: THANK GOODNESS.

436
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:23,137
YOU DON’T KNOW
HOW GRATEFUL I AM,

437
00:20:23,137 --> 00:20:25,757
ELITE DISCIPLE EUGEO, SIR!

438
00:20:25,757 --> 00:20:27,307
Eugeo: YOUR WORK’S
DONE FOR TODAY,

439
00:20:27,307 --> 00:20:29,227
SO PLEASE JUST CALL ME EUGEO.

440
00:20:29,227 --> 00:20:32,727
ANYWAY, THERE’S SOMETHING
I NEED TO APOLOGIZE FOR.

441
00:20:34,267 --> 00:20:35,937
I WASN’T SURE OF IT YESTERDAY,

442
00:20:35,937 --> 00:20:38,737
BUT NOW I AM.

443
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:40,987
THE REASON THIS HAPPENED
IN THE FIRST PLACE

444
00:20:40,987 --> 00:20:44,827
WAS ALL BECAUSE OF THE DUEL
I HAD WITH HUMBERT.

445
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:48,537
DO YOU THINK YOU COULD SET UP
A MEETING WITH HER FOR ME?

446
00:20:48,537 --> 00:20:51,497
I’D LIKE TO APOLOGIZE IN PERSON.

447
00:20:51,497 --> 00:20:53,497
( Tiese gasps )

448
00:20:53,497 --> 00:20:56,207
YES. OF COURSE.

449
00:20:56,207 --> 00:20:58,667
HONESTLY, DESPITE WHAT YOU SAY,

450
00:20:58,667 --> 00:21:00,877
NONE OF THIS
IS REALLY YOUR FAULT.

451
00:21:00,877 --> 00:21:02,297
BUT I’LL BE MORE THAN HAPPY

452
00:21:02,297 --> 00:21:05,047
TO CONVEY YOUR WISHES TO HER,
NONE THE LESS.

453
00:21:05,047 --> 00:21:07,887
UM, C-COULD I...

454
00:21:07,887 --> 00:21:09,017
Eugeo: MM?

455
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:11,227
Tiese: C-COULD I
SIT CLOSER TO YOU?

456
00:21:11,227 --> 00:21:13,647
Eugeo: UH...

457
00:21:13,647 --> 00:21:14,857
SURE.

458
00:21:22,527 --> 00:21:24,027
Tiese: I’VE BEEN THINKING.

459
00:21:24,027 --> 00:21:26,867
AFTER I GRADUATE
FROM THE ACADEMY,

460
00:21:26,867 --> 00:21:29,997
I’LL TAKE OVER AS HEAD
OF THE SCHTRINEN FAMILY.

461
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:33,287
AS IS CUSTOM, I WILL THEN
HAVE TO MARRY A NOBLE

462
00:21:33,287 --> 00:21:35,577
WHO IS OF THE SAME RANK
OR POSSIBLY HIGHER.

463
00:21:39,877 --> 00:21:41,007
AND IT TERRIFIES ME!

464
00:21:41,007 --> 00:21:42,587
( Eugeo gasps )

465
00:21:42,587 --> 00:21:44,717
Tiese: WHAT IF THE MAN
WHO BECOMES MY HUSBAND

466
00:21:44,717 --> 00:21:47,547
TURNS OUT TO BE
SOMEONE LIKE LORD ZIZEK,

467
00:21:47,547 --> 00:21:49,467
SOMEONE WHO IS CRUEL TO OTHERS

468
00:21:49,467 --> 00:21:51,727
AND WHO LACKS
THE BASIC PRINCIPLES OF HONOR

469
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:53,937
MY FATHER RAISED ME TO UPHOLD?

470
00:21:53,937 --> 00:21:56,057
I’M SO SCARED.

471
00:21:56,057 --> 00:21:57,477
WHAT DO I DO?

472
00:22:03,107 --> 00:22:04,107
( Eugeo gasps )

473
00:22:04,107 --> 00:22:06,867
♪

474
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,447
TIESE.

475
00:22:08,447 --> 00:22:11,617
Tiese: EUGEO, IF--
IF IT WOULD BE ALL RIGHT,

476
00:22:11,617 --> 00:22:13,957
I’D LIKE TO ASK
ANOTHER FAVOR OF YOU.

477
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:16,367
I HAVE NO DOUBT THAT EVENTUALLY

478
00:22:16,367 --> 00:22:18,787
YOU’LL RISE
TO THE TOP OF OUR CLASS,

479
00:22:18,787 --> 00:22:20,337
WIN THE SWORDSMANSHIP
TOURNAMENT,

480
00:22:20,337 --> 00:22:23,667
AND COMPETE IN THE FOUR EMPIRE
UNIFICATION TOURNAMENT.

481
00:22:23,667 --> 00:22:25,337
Eugeo: UH, I HOPE TO.

482
00:22:25,337 --> 00:22:28,677
I MEAN, I AM WORKING HARD
TOWARD THAT GOAL.

483
00:22:28,677 --> 00:22:33,137
Tiese: AND THEN,
AFTER THAT, IF YOU--

484
00:22:33,137 --> 00:22:36,807
IF YOU RANK HIGH
IN THE UNIFICATION TOURNAMENT,

485
00:22:36,807 --> 00:22:39,807
I HEARD YOU CAN BE
APPOINTED AS A NOBLE.

486
00:22:39,807 --> 00:22:42,777
THAT’S WHAT HAPPENED WITH
OUR SUPERVISOR, MS. AZURICA.

487
00:22:42,777 --> 00:22:46,487
AND THEN, IF YOU DO
DECIDE TO TAKE A TITLE,

488
00:22:46,487 --> 00:22:50,697
DO YOU THINK--
WOULD YOU BE MY--

489
00:22:50,697 --> 00:22:53,367
♪

490
00:22:53,367 --> 00:22:56,867
Eugeo: I’M NOT HERE
FOR THE TOURNAMENT.

491
00:22:56,867 --> 00:22:59,167
I’M DOING THIS
TO BECOME AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT

492
00:22:59,167 --> 00:23:00,167
AND FIND ALICE,

493
00:23:00,167 --> 00:23:02,457
BUT I CAN’T TELL HER THAT.

494
00:23:05,627 --> 00:23:07,127
( sighs )

495
00:23:07,127 --> 00:23:09,007
IT’S OKAY.

496
00:23:09,007 --> 00:23:11,967
AFTER THE TOURNAMENT,
WE’LL TALK MORE ABOUT THIS.

497
00:23:11,967 --> 00:23:14,517
Tiese: I’LL BE WAITING,

498
00:23:14,517 --> 00:23:16,807
AND I’LL WORK AS HARD AS YOU!

499
00:23:16,807 --> 00:23:19,347
I WANT TO BECOME STRONG ENOUGH

500
00:23:19,347 --> 00:23:23,147
SO THAT I CAN SPEAK UP
FOR WHAT IS RIGHT.

501
00:23:23,147 --> 00:23:25,107
JUST LIKE YOU, EUGEO.

502
00:23:25,107 --> 00:23:28,487
Singer: ♪ THE IRIS TO YOU ♪
